  "id": "Compound::DB00714 - Gene::1812",
  "verbalization": "Apomorphine is linked to Drd1 through a shared pathway involving the Dopamine Neurotransmitter Receptor Activity, coupled via Gs. This relationship is supported by multiple evidence paths, all of which indicate that Apomorphine binds to Drd4, which in turn participates in Dopamine Neurotransmitter Receptor Activity, coupled via Gs. This activity is then participated by Drd1, suggesting a functional connection between Apomorphine and Drd1 through the dopamine signaling cascade. The evidence highlights a mechanism where Apomorphine may modulate Drd1 activity via Drd4, potentially influencing dopamine receptor function. The consistent presence of Drd4 and Drd1 in the same pathway, along with the involvement of Gs-coupled dopamine receptors, supports a role for Apomorphine in regulating Drd1 through dopamine signaling. The integration of these paths underscores a core mechanism where Apomorphine's interaction with Drd4 leads to a downstream effect on Drd1, likely through the dopamine receptor system.",
